A class-level :DECLARE after the first method: fields belong before the
methods that use them (diag.class_member_order, info tier, so it appears
only under --info). Method-local :DECLARE statements inside a body never
count.
-- input.ssl --
:CLASS Tally;
:INHERIT Lab.Counter;
:DECLARE nTotal;

:PROCEDURE Add;
	:PARAMETERS nDelta;
	:DECLARE nOld;
	nOld := Me:nTotal;
	Me:nTotal := nOld + nDelta;
:ENDPROC;

:DECLARE nLastDelta;

:PROCEDURE Last;
	:RETURN Me:nLastDelta;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:CLASS Tally;
:INHERIT Lab.Counter;
:DECLARE nTotal;

:PROCEDURE Add;
	:PARAMETERS nDelta;
	:DECLARE nOld;

	nOld := Me:nTotal;
	Me:nTotal := nOld + nDelta;
:ENDPROC;

:DECLARE nLastDelta;

:PROCEDURE Last;
	:RETURN Me:nLastDelta;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
12:1-12:9 info class_member_order: Class members must be ordered as ':DECLARE' fields, then methods
